Asset Health Observatory is an evidence-bound facility asset health observation
runtime for DCCP Tranche 1. It owns observation, explanation, history, evidence
correlation, and explicit risk and degradation views. It does not own asset
registry identity, hardware lifecycle transitions, maintenance scheduling,
firmware authority, incidents, quarantine, replacement, or actuation. It is
built from the C++20 standard library and the operating system's own primitives.

Third-party components
----------------------

None. No third-party source code, library, header, or generated artefact is
included in, linked into, or required by this product.

The build depends only on the platform's own toolchain and operating system:

  * the C++20 standard library of the toolchain that builds the project;
  * the operating system's cryptographic random generator, reached through the
    platform API (BCryptGenRandom on Windows, /dev/urandom elsewhere), used for
    evidence and store identifiers;
  * the operating system's file, directory and locking primitives, used for the
    durable store (CreateFileW, WriteFile, FlushFileBuffers, MoveFileExW and
    LockFileEx on Windows; open, write, fsync, rename and flock elsewhere).

No network service, telemetry endpoint, analytics library, or runtime package
manager is contacted or required at build time or at run time. This product
transmits nothing.

Evidence and data
-----------------

The test suite and the benchmarks generate their own evidence. No facility
instrument, building management system, DCIM system, electrical or cooling device
was involved in producing any result in this repository. What has been proven,
and what has not, is stated explicitly in README.md.

